# AI
# `.claude/` stays out of git, and the reason is sharper than "local state".
#
# Two different things get called "a skill here". A skill that ships to
# CONSUMERS of agent-bus is settled and refused (6d23091, 856551b, bab45e4):
# it cross-installs into other harnesses without asking, it pins itself near
# the system prompt for the whole session, and it does not go down with the
# MCP server it describes -- so a stale copy outlives the thing it documents.
# The MCP server is the only sane surface for instructing a consumer.
#
# A skill WE use to maintain this repo is a different thing and not that. But
# committing one still puts it in every clone and every fork, and ours name
# `project 4` and owner `danbarua` in five places -- so a fork would hand its
# contributors a skill pointing at somebody else's board. Ours are ours:
# keep them in ~/.claude/skills/ or untracked here.
.claude/

